  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Emergency Grant Aid in Response to the Deterioration of the Humanitarian Situation in Belarus</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">For several months, increased numbers of crossings of migrants from Belarus into the European Union (EU) have been observed. Considering the political impasse and the rapidly worsening weather in Belarus, it is of extreme urgency for humanitarian actors to step up and support stranded migrants in Belarus and at the borders with the EU, while at the same time providing viable alternative solutions for the migrants. In response, IOM aims to contribute to the provision of life-saving humanitarian aid and offer emergency health and viable and sustainable protection solutions to the stranded migrants. This project also supports the Belarusian authorities to address the exceptional circumstances and needs of a migrant population that finds itself stranded in the country.</narrative>
  </description>
